      "content": "Got it, so we'd weight those cohesion metrics. Following that logic, if we're training the model on historical data, how do we prevent it from just creating a feedback loop where certain neighborhoods are always flagged as 'high risk' simply because they have high concentrations of specific minority groups or lower socioeconomic backgrounds? Essentially, if the historical data shows more policing or more incidents in those areas, won't the model just conclude that those specific demographics are inherently linked to higher instability? How do you handle that bias in the data so the heat map is actually predictive rather than just reinforcing existing patterns?",
